 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the executive law, in relation to designating Great Valley as an inland waterway for purposes of waterfront revitalization",
    "basePrintNo": "S6821",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6821-2017",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §911, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6821\n\n TITLE OF BILL :\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to designating Great\nValley as an inland waterway for purposes of waterfront revitalization\n\n PURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL :\n\nTo add waterways in the Town and Village of Ellicottville to the list\nof Designated Inland Waterways.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nAmends Section 1, Subdivision 4, Article 42 of Section 911 of\nExecutive Law, to expand the definition of inland waterways to include\nthe Great Valley Creek in the Town of Ellicottville.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nThe Town and Village of Ellicottville intends to create a Local\nWaterfront Revitalization Plan. Creating such a plan would help\nEllicottville designate development and preservation plans that would\nthen allow them to apply for government funding streams to support\nEllicottville's growth and sustainability. Adding the Great Valley to\nthe list of Designated Waterways would make the communities along the\nwaterway eligible for funding from the Environmental Protection Fund\n(EPF) Local Waterfront Revitalization Program (LWRP) to carry out this\nplan. In addition, in order for a locality to receive a grant from the\nDepartment of State (DOS) for the Local Waterfront Revitalization\nPlan, the Legislature must pass a bill that would add the locality's\nwaterways to the list of Designated Waterways.  Therefore, passage of\nthis bill is necessary for Ellicottville to receive a DOS grant.\n\n PRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNew Bill.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS :\n\nNone.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nImmediately.\n",
    "multiSponsors": {
