    "lawCode": "Amd §911, Exec L",
    "lawSection": "Executive Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S6821A\n\nSPONSOR: YOUNG\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the executive law, in relation to designating Great\nValley as an inland waterway for purposes of waterfront revitalization\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo add waterways in the Town and Village of Ellicottville to the list of\nDesignated Inland Waterways.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nAmends Paragraph c of Subdivision 4 of Section 911 of Executive Law, as\nseparately amended by chapters 43, 110, 142, 161, and 255 of the laws of\n2017, to expand the definition of inland waterways to include the Great\nValley Creek in the Town of Ellicottville.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThe Town and Village of Ellicottville intends to create a Local Water-\nfront Revitalization Plan. Creating such a plan would help Ellicottville\ndesignate development and preservation plans that would then allow them\nto apply for government funding streams to support Ellicottville's\ngrowth and sustainability. Adding the Great Valley to the list of Desig-\nnated Waterways would make the communities along the waterway eligible\nfor funding from the Environmental Protection Fund (EPF) Local Water-\nfront Revitalization Program (LWRP) to carry out this plan. In addition,\nin order for a locality to receive a grant from the Department of State\n(DOS) for the Local Waterfront Revitalization Plan, the Legislature must\npass a bill that would add the locality's waterways to the list of\nDesignated Waterways.  Therefore, passage of this bill is necessary for\nEllicottville to receive a DOS grant.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2017: S.6821/A.8355A Referred to Rules\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
